  "summary": "video-use is an open-source skill that lets an LLM agent (Claude Code, Codex, etc.) edit raw video footage conversationally via ffmpeg/PIL helper scripts, transcript-driven cut planning, and a self-eval render loop. Evidence covers its helper tooling, EDL interface, memory file, sub-agent orchestration, dependencies, and agent-facing install workflow. Evidence coverage: 137 of 141 packet slices were shown to the model; the rest were withheld by the prompt budget.",
